## Run

Create an environment with Python 3.10 or newer, then install dependencies and run:

```powershell
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
python train.py
python evaluate.py
```

The split is seeded and stored in `outputs/reports/split.json`. `train.py` fits each
selected model on training rows only and saves model artifacts. `evaluate.py` computes
metrics from the held-out rows and saves JSON reports and the selected figures under
`outputs/`.

Edit `experiment.yaml` to preserve the experiment configuration. The generated
scripts read it at runtime, so changes to the task, selected columns, models, split,
seed, metrics, and outputs remain explicit and reviewable.